{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "Apache Airflow REST API (DAGs, DAG runs, task instances, variables, connections)",
    "version": "3.1.8",
    "description": "Trimmed by a script from apache/airflow at tag 3.1.8 (airflow-core/src/airflow/api_fastapi/core_api/openapi/v2-rest-api-generated.yaml, read 2026-11-01), the version STACKIT Workflows' `workflows-3.0-airflow-3.1` names, to the DAG, DAG run, task instance, variable and connection routes the provider's bindings need. STACKIT publishes no document for this API. Changes from the source, all to describe the wire: OpenAPI 3.1 `anyOf: [X, null]` is 3.0 `nullable`; schema titles are gone; a task instance's `trigger` and `triggerer_job` stay open objects; security schemes are gone, because a session cookie is what the protocol sends; the listing routes keep only `limit`, `offset`, `state`, `order_by` and one narrowing filter each; the failure responses share one schema, because FastAPI's `detail` is text on an HTTPException and a list on validation. A variable's `value` is a string where upstream has any JSON value, because the image answered 500 to an object on PATCH. The connection PATCH route's path parameter is `connection_key` where upstream has `connection_id`, which only renames it here: the body needs its own `connection_id`, and one name can't be both. The update_mask parameter of the PATCH routes isn't kept: without it they leave what the body omits alone. Bodies and status codes were checked by running each request against the apache/airflow:3.1.8 image with a `_token` cookie, read 2026-11-01. STACKIT's own instances have not been probed: that `endpoints.url` serves this API, and that its session endpoint's cookie works on Airflow 3, are inferred from STACKIT's concepts page, whose example only calls `/api/v1/dags`."
  },
